<title>USA: Auburn, Wash., schools repriced, yields raised.</title>
<headline>Auburn, Wash., schools repriced, yields raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seattle-Northwest Securities Corp said Tuesday it repriced Auburn School District No 408, Wash.'s $38 million bond deal, raising yields in the 2012 through 2014 maturities.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>AUBURN SCHOOL DISTRICT #408</p>
<p>KING COUNTY, WASH.</p>
<p>1997</p>
<p>DATED: 3/1/1997  DUE: 6/1 &amp; 12/1 FIRST COUPON: 6/1/1997</p>
<p>RATING: Aaa/AAA AMBAC (1997-2009, 2011, 2013)</p>
<p>UNDERLYING: A-1/A-plus (2010-2012, 2014-2016)</p>
<p>AWARD: 2/26/1997</p>
<p>DELIVERY: 3/13/1997</p>
<p>CALL: 12/1/2007 AT 100.00</p>
<p>2008, 2009 NON CALLABLE</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>			Amount	  Coupon	Price</p>
<p>    Maturity	(million)	   (pct)	 (% of par)</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>6/1</p>
<p>    1997	    $0.350	  4.00	  3.50</p>
<p>    1998	    $1.100	  4.00	  3.80</p>
<p>    1999	    $0.250	  4.10	  100</p>
<p>    2000	    $0.300	  4.20	  100</p>
<p>    2001	    $0.400	  4.25	  4.30</p>
